## 2. MODIFY `web/src/persistence/section-registry.ts` — implement merge

Currently every `write` throws on non-`replace` (`requireReplace` helper + `str
ingArraySetter`
helper). Implement real merge. Make exactly these changes — nothing else in the
file:

**(a) Delete the `requireReplace` helper** (no longer used after this change).

**(b) Add these helpers** near the top (after the type defs). They are delibera
tely
**type-tolerant**: `migrateCampaign` validates the envelope wrapper but section
payloads are
`unknown`, so a structurally-valid file with a wrong-typed section (e.g. `annot
ations:"x"`,
`featureNotes:[]`) must NOT crash the import or write garbage — it falls back t
o existing/empty.
(The store `load*()` sanitizers still run on the post-import reload, so corrupt
-but-typed entries
are cleaned then.)

```ts
function asArray<T>(v: unknown): T[] {
  return Array.isArray(v) ? (v as T[]) : []
}
function asRecord(v: unknown): Record<string, unknown> {
  return v !== null && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v) ? (v as Recor
d<string, unknown>) : {}
}

function dedupeFirst(ids: string[]): string[] {
  const seen = new Set<string>()
  const out: string[] = []
  for (const id of ids) {
    if (typeof id !== 'string' || seen.has(id)) continue
    seen.add(id)
    out.push(id)
  }
  return out
}

// Merge arrays of identified records: existing order preserved, incoming wins 
on id collision,
// new incoming records appended. Items without a string id are skipped (tolera
nt of corrupt input).
function mergeById<T extends { id: string }>(existing: T[], incoming: T[]): T[]
{
  const map = new Map<string, T>()
  for (const item of existing) if (item && typeof (item as { id?: unknown }).id
=== 'string') map.set(item.id, item)
  for (const item of incoming) if (item && typeof (item as { id?: unknown }).id
=== 'string') map.set(item.id, item)
  return [...map.values()]
}
```

**(c) Replace the `stringArraySetter` helper** so it handles merge (set-union).
It must take the
getter too. (The old `key` param was unused — drop it.)

```ts
function stringArraySetter(
  getter: () => string[],
  setter: (ids: string[]) => void,
): CampaignSection<string[]>['write'] {
  return (value, mode) => {
    const incoming = asArray<string>(value)
    setter(mode === 'merge' ? dedupeFirst([...getter(), ...incoming]) : dedupeF
irst(incoming))
  }
}
```
(`dedupeFirst` on the replace path too keeps the strings-only invariant regardl
ess of which setter
runs — the helper now owns deduplication; `setPrepOrder` no longer needs a call
er to pre-dedupe.)

Update its three call sites accordingly:
- stars: `write: stringArraySetter(getStarredIds, setStarredIds)`
- prepOrder: `write: stringArraySetter(getPrepOrder, setPrepOrder)`
- prepDone: `write: stringArraySetter(getPrepDoneIds, setPrepDoneIds)`

**(d) Array-by-id content sections** — annotations, journeys, layerPresets. Rep
lace each `write`:

```ts
// annotations
write(value, mode) {
  const incoming = asArray(value) as ReturnType<typeof loadAnnotations>
  saveAnnotations(mode === 'merge' ? mergeById(loadAnnotations(), incoming) : i
ncoming)
},
```
…and identically for `journeys` (loadSavedJourneys/saveJourneys) and `layerPres
ets`
(loadCustomPresets/saveCustomPresets). (All three element types have a string `
id`.)

**(e) Record content sections** — featureNotes, featureHooks. Replace each `wri
te`:

```ts
// featureNotes
write(value, mode) {
  const incoming = asRecord(value) as ReturnType<typeof loadFeatureNotes>
  saveFeatureNotes(mode === 'merge' ? { ...loadFeatureNotes(), ...incoming } : 
incoming)
},
```
…and identically for `featureHooks` (loadFeatureHooks/saveFeatureHooks). (Sprea
d = incoming wins
per key; existing keys absent from the file are preserved.)

**(f) Preference sections** — these are only ever called with `mode === 'replac
e'` (the importer
skips preferences on merge), so mode is irrelevant; just call the setter. (Omit
ting the second
`mode` parameter is valid TS — a 1-arg function is assignable to the 2-arg `wri
te` member type.)

```ts
// timeOfDay
write(value) { saveTimeOfDay(value as ReturnType<typeof loadTimeOfDay>) },
// hexSize
write(value) { saveHexSize(value as ReturnType<typeof loadHexSize>) },
```

**(g) 🔒 aiLoreSettings.write — SECURITY-CRITICAL.** Export strips `apiKey`, so
the incoming
settings have no key. The write MUST preserve the user's existing local key (ne
ver clobber it
with the absent property):

```ts
// aiLoreSettings
write(value) {
  const incoming = value as AiLoreSettings
  saveAiLoreSettings({ ...incoming, apiKey: loadAiLoreSettings().apiKey })
},
```

Leave every section's `read()` and the section list/order exactly as-is.

