`e.target.value=''`
  reset after pick).

Behavior:
- **Save campaign:** `const data = JSON.stringify(exportCampaign(), null, 2)` (
import
  `exportCampaign` from `../persistence/campaign-export`) → Blob (`type: 'appli
cation/json'`) →
  download as `veydria-campaign-${new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10)}.json`. 
Then
  `onToast?.('Campaign saved')`. Close the dropdown.
  Add a one-line comment: `// Phase 6: reroute through Tauri save dialog.`
- **Open campaign / Import & merge:** both use **one** hidden
  `<input type="file" accept=".json" multiple={false}>` with a ref + a `pending
ModeRef`
  (`'open' | 'import'`). Clicking the dropdown row **closes the dropdown first*
*, sets the pending
  mode, and `.click()`s the input (so a cancelled file pick — which fires no `o
nChange` — leaves a
  clean closed state). `onChange`: read the file via `await file.text()`, then
  `try { const parsed = JSON.parse(text) }`; open a confirm modal with state
  `{ mode, filename, parsed?, error? }` (error = the JSON parse error message).
Reset `e.target.value=''`.
- **Confirm modal:** a simple fixed-overlay modal (style it minimally with inli
ne styles or reuse a
  modal class if one exists — keep it visually consistent, do NOT add a global 
CSS file). Contents:
  - Title: `Open campaign?` (replace) or `Import & merge?`.
  - Warning text: for open — *"This replaces your current annotations, journeys
, notes, stars,
    prep, hooks, and layer presets with the contents of {filename}."*; for impo
rt — *"This merges
    {filename} into your current campaign (existing items are kept; matching it
ems are updated)."*
  - If there is an `error`, show it inline in a warning style and **disable** t
he confirm button.
  - Buttons: **Cancel** (closes modal) and **Open**/**Import** (confirm).
  - Confirm handler:
    ```ts
    try {
      importCampaign(parsed, mode === 'open' ? 'replace' : 'merge')
      window.location.reload()   // re-hydrate; imported state renders fresh
    } catch (e) {
      setError(e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e))   // show inline, ke
ep modal open
    }
    ```
    (import `importCampaign` + `type ImportMode` are not needed here; pass the 
literal mode.)
- Close the modal/dropdown on Escape and on overlay click.

**Accessibility (match the share-popover bar, plus modal essentials):** modal i
s
`role="dialog" aria-modal="true"` with an `aria-label` (the title) and `aria-de
scribedby` pointing
at the warning text. On open, move focus to the safe default button (Cancel); o
n close, return
focus to the "Campaign ▾" trigger. Escape closes. (A full focus-trap is NOT req
uired — it exceeds
the app's current bar; the share-popover has none. Arrow-key dropdown navigatio
n is likewise not
required, matching the existing share-menu.)

